{"sample_id": 27, "prompt": "CELEBRATIONS reminds us to celebrate the seasons of our lives. Remember the summer fresh-g", "reference": "arden herbs and vegetables, the familiar tastes of autumn apples from the orchard just down the road?\nWhisperings of winter, remind us of the cozy meals that once comforted and soothed. We need time to feast from tables set with traditions and to gather with those we love.\nSimple, yet savory recipes that seem familiar to us from childhood are the heart of classic meals. As we savor these familiar aromas, the feelings from special gatherings from long ago are reborn, as old things become new again.\nSome of the treasured recipes given to author by close friends and family are included in this compilation of favorites. Enjoy Roasted Pepper Chicken on Ciabatta or Ginger Glazed Salmon Stir Fry with Wild Berry Pistachio Salad and a Tuxedo Brownie Square.......all delicious!\nWe hope you will use Celebrations as a guide to enjoy simple afternoon luncheons, sunday afternoon games, birthday parties, anniversaries, or even the birth of a newborn baby.", "generated_dual_stream": "ardeners, and the winter indoor/outdoor enthusiasts alike. Well, CELEBRATIONS is often a celebration of the seasons when it comes to the gardeners, the winter indoor/outdoor enthusiasts alike. Well, CELEBRATIONS is one of", "generated_original": "rown fruits, the holidays with friends and family, and the snow-covered landscapes of winter. As you look back over the past year, look for the lessons you learned and the joy you felt. Then look forward to the next year and celebrate the new", "metrics_dual_stream": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.11398963730569948, "rouge2": 0.010471204188481674, "rougeL": 0.10362694300518135, "rougeLsum": 0.11398963730569948}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.38095238095238093, 0.04878048780487805, 0.0, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 0.034834644453412465, "length_ratio": 0.22950819672131148, "translation_length": 42, "reference_length": 183}, "bert_score_precision": 0.7977621555328369, "bert_score_recall": 0.7777738571166992, "bert_score_f1": 0.7876412272453308}, "metrics_original": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.19607843137254902, "rouge2": 0.0297029702970297, "rougeL": 0.11764705882352941, "rougeLsum": 0.18627450980392155}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.5102040816326531, 0.10416666666666667, 0.02127659574468085, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 0.06491387565719794, "length_ratio": 0.2677595628415301, "translation_length": 49, "reference_length": 183}, "bert_score_precision": 0.8532265424728394, "bert_score_recall": 0.8006116151809692, "bert_score_f1": 0.826082170009613}, "original_model_loss_on_full_text": 3.3389599323272705}
{"sample_id": 28, "prompt": "Free Season Ticket and Boyds Boots?\nA.G.M. covering the 31st May ", "reference": "2009 ending Accounts.\nTickets Prices For Next Year????", "generated_dual_stream": "2018 crossing the first 11 years old. All our sale now!\nM.C. Councillor for the 2018-2019 crossing the first 11 years old! All our ticket sales now!\nA.G.M. covering the first", "generated_original": "2018.\nWe are looking for a new Chairman.\nWe are looking for new Directors.", "metrics_dual_stream": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.04651162790697674, "rouge2": 0.0, "rougeL": 0.04651162790697674, "rougeLsum": 0.04651162790697674}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.022222222222222223, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 1.0, "length_ratio": 3.4615384615384617, "translation_length": 45, "reference_length": 13}, "bert_score_precision": 0.8291998505592346, "bert_score_recall": 0.8459786176681519, "bert_score_f1": 0.8375051617622375}, "metrics_original": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.09090909090909091, "rouge2": 0.0, "rougeL": 0.09090909090909091, "rougeLsum": 0.09090909090909091}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.058823529411764705, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 1.0, "length_ratio": 1.3076923076923077, "translation_length": 17, "reference_length": 13}, "bert_score_precision": 0.8504223823547363, "bert_score_recall": 0.8377007246017456, "bert_score_f1": 0.8440135717391968}, "original_model_loss_on_full_text": 5.412243843078613}
{"sample_id": 29, "prompt": "Consider replacing the flapper and inspect the inside of the tank to see if there is any build", "reference": "-up preventing a proper seal. Also inspect the lift wire/guide to see if it is bent, corroded or catching on something, preventing the flapper from closing properly.\nThe float arm needs to be adjusted so that the water level is 2\" below the top of the overflow pipe. The float arm may need to be repositioned to obtain the desired water level. If it is a plastic float arm, adjust the screw located at the top of the arm. Also make sure the refill tube is located about 1/4\" over the overflow pipe. If necessary, clip the tube to the overflow pipe to stabilize it and keep it from moving into the overflow pipe.\nConsider replacing or repairing the service line to prevent larger loss of water. A professional service may need to be contacted for completing this task.\nAt this point, try to determine where the water is going inside the home.\nFinally, if all of the above tests show no evidence of leaked water, check the appliances that cycle. Water softeners can cause an increase in usage, so check the settings to make sure it is not cycling more often than necessary and monitor its full cycle to make sure it is operating properly. Also check outside spigots and hydrants to make sure they are not dripping, especially when connected to a sprinkler, soaker hose, or irrigation system. Take note of the times when extra water may be used, possibly weekends and evenings, when watering plants and gardens.\nCheck out our Conservation Tips under News & Notices for more suggestions.", "generated_dual_stream": "-up or decay. The bottom of the tank to see if the tank has a leak. You can also replace the tank with long-lasting white to prevent corrosion on your body and body parts. The tank color on the tank will also be useful for you", "generated_original": "up of sediments and debris. If there is, clean the tank using a mild detergent and a soft brush. Fill the tank with fresh water and let the filter run for 15 minutes to clear the tank of debris.", "metrics_dual_stream": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.14193548387096772, "rouge2": 0.025974025974025972, "rougeL": 0.1096774193548387, "rougeLsum": 0.12258064516129032}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.46938775510204084, 0.125, 0.02127659574468085, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 0.006468465782215207, "length_ratio": 0.16554054054054054, "translation_length": 49, "reference_length": 296}, "bert_score_precision": 0.8672422170639038, "bert_score_recall": 0.8106497526168823, "bert_score_f1": 0.8379915952682495}, "metrics_original": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.11258278145695363, "rouge2": 0.0, "rougeL": 0.07947019867549669, "rougeLsum": 0.11258278145695363}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.46511627906976744, 0.023809523809523808, 0.0, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 0.002784405397389782, "length_ratio": 0.14527027027027026, "translation_length": 43, "reference_length": 296}, "bert_score_precision": 0.8512448072433472, "bert_score_recall": 0.8111879229545593, "bert_score_f1": 0.8307338356971741}, "original_model_loss_on_full_text": 2.4528653621673584}
{"sample_id": 30, "prompt": "LEWISTON \u2014 The Calvary United Medthodist Church will hold its monthly bean", "reference": " supper at 4:45 p.m. Saturday, April 13, at the church on Sabattus Street.\nThe meal will include bakes beans, hot dogs, salads, casseroles (including vegetarian), biscuits, brown bread and pies. Cost is $8 for adults and $3 for children under 10.\nUse the Garden Entrance on Bartlett Street. For more information, call Lucky DiBello at 207-784-3869.\nPERU \u2014 The Rumford Senior Citizens will hold an Easter Luncheon at 11:30 a.m. Monday, April 15, at the old Peru Elementary School, 1 Main St.\nCost is $6. This event is open to the public. There are only 40 seats available, so call ahead to make reservations.\nFor more information or to reserve seating, call 207-562-7700.", "generated_dual_stream": ", wine and other related meals from 5:30 to 6:30 p.m. on Aug. 16 at the church\u2019s facility in Lewiston. The meals will be served.\nThe church will be closed on the day of the meeting", "generated_original": "supper from 5 to 7 p.m. Friday, April 13, at 17 Main St. The menu includes meat loaf, green beans and mashed potatoes, dessert and drink. All proceeds benefit the church\u2019s youth group, youth ministry and", "metrics_dual_stream": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.21383647798742142, "rouge2": 0.038216560509554146, "rougeL": 0.13836477987421383, "rougeLsum": 0.20125786163522014}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.008020539986087346, "precisions": [0.5434782608695652, 0.13333333333333333, 0.045454545454545456, 0.023255813953488372], "brevity_penalty": 0.08573263342266117, "length_ratio": 0.2893081761006289, "translation_length": 46, "reference_length": 159}, "bert_score_precision": 0.8896112442016602, "bert_score_recall": 0.8161993026733398, "bert_score_f1": 0.8513255715370178}, "metrics_original": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.189873417721519, "rouge2": 0.06410256410256411, "rougeL": 0.13924050632911392, "rougeLsum": 0.189873417721519}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.015458714622916