{"sample_id": 41, "prompt": "Kalanchoe is an eye-catching succulent, displaying large heads of bright orange flowers during", "reference": " the winter. Ideal for basket or pot, the Kalanchoe thrives outdoors in a sheltered position, protected from frost. Alternatively, bring the cheerful colour indoors and choose a warm, brightly lit spot. Don\u2019t over water; allow plant to dry out a little between watering. Ideal for containers and sunny, hot spots in the garden.\nThese plants have been selected and grown in W.A. to suit local conditions and for their outstanding water wise feature.\nHandle with CARE. Plants are not suitable for human or animal consumption.", "generated_dual_stream": "your tour. To make sure your flowers last, they are all edible. The branches include fruit that takes shape. They also sell attractive pods that are edible. The plants, also known as \u201cKalanchoe\u201d, are native to the South", "generated_original": "summer. This is a very low maintenance plant, and it is drought-tolerant. It does well in either bright or dim light. The plant is native to the deserts of Africa, and it is considered a tough plant.\nHow to Grow", "metrics_dual_stream": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.128, "rouge2": 0.0, "rougeL": 0.08, "rougeLsum": 0.128}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.24444444444444444, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 0.28176928909495835, "length_ratio": 0.4411764705882353, "translation_length": 45, "reference_length": 102}, "bert_score_precision": 0.857468843460083, "bert_score_recall": 0.8289214372634888, "bert_score_f1": 0.8429535031318665}, "metrics_original": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.171875, "rouge2": 0.0, "rougeL": 0.125, "rougeLsum": 0.15625}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.34782608695652173, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 0.2960013380148583, "length_ratio": 0.45098039215686275, "translation_length": 46, "reference_length": 102}, "bert_score_precision": 0.8749989867210388, "bert_score_recall": 0.8386820554733276, "bert_score