{"sample_id": 57, "prompt": "Ankylosing spondylitis is an inflammatory disease that over time can cause vertebral fusion", "reference": " in the spine. This fusion makes the spine less flexible and can lead to a curved posture forward. When the ribs are touched, it can be difficult to breathe deeply. Ankylosing spondylitis affects men more than women. Signs and symptoms usually begin in early adulthood. Inflammation can also occur in other parts of the body, most often in the eyes. Ankylosing spondylitis cannot be cured, but treatments can reduce their symptoms and possibly delay the progression of the disease. It is a type of arthritis which especially affects the spine. Mostly men at their teen age get attack by this disease.\nIts actual causing reason is still unknown. But it is hypothesized that some genes like HLA-B27 may be responsible for developing this disease.", "generated_dual_stream": "to occur in the spine.\nAnky, as you\u2019re no doubt, refers to the spine. Spongy, as you know, means around. It\u2019s a disease that can cause chronic pain and stiffness throughout the spine and hips. When chronic", "generated_original": "(spinal fusion), and spinal deformity (kyphosis) due to progressive inflammation of the spine. Ankylosing spondylitis may occur in isolation or as part of a constellation of symptoms that are referred to as the HLA-B", "metrics_dual_stream": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.2195121951219512, "rouge2": 0.0617283950617284, "rougeL": 0.12195121951219512, "rougeLsum": 0.17073170731707318}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.014263232368010593, "precisions": [0.5333333333333333, 0.18181818181818182, 0.06976744186046512, 0.023809523809523808], "brevity_penalty": 0.1266071027890836, "length_ratio": 0.32608695652173914, "translation_length": 45, "reference_length": 138}, "bert_score_precision": 0.8402640223503113, "bert_score_recall": 0.8268131613731384, "bert_score_f1": 0.8334843516349792}, "metrics_original": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.2625, "rouge2": 0.05063291139240506