{"sample_id": 532, "prompt": "To clean the handle of your brushes, pour rubbing alcohol onto a cotton pad and rub over the", "reference": " handle of your brushes. This will not only clean but also disinfect the handles. Yay! This will not only clean but also disinfect the handles.... I am so hard on brushes. I can keep them clean, that's not the issue. It's the'scumbling' that wrecks my brushes...wears them down to a stubby shadow of their former selves.\nIn the middle of a painting project and want to keep your brushes fresh overnight? In this case, there\u2019s no need to give them a thorough clean.", "generated_dual_stream": "bristles. This will remove the residue from the brush and the handle and can be replaced with a new grip. The alcohol can be replaced with a new grip and the handle can be replaced for a new grip. You can use a new grip for", "generated_original": "brush handle. Dry with a lint-free cloth or paper towel.\nTo clean your makeup brushes, put them in a plastic bag or basket and mix in a solution of 1 part isopropyl alcohol and 1 part water.\nA clean makeup", "metrics_dual_stream": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.19402985074626866, "rouge2": 0.015151515151515152, "rougeL": 0.1492537313432836, "rougeLsum": 0.1791044776119403}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.30612244897959184, 0.041666666666666664, 0.02127659574468085, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 0.3460318383532258, "length_ratio": 0.48514851485148514, "translation_length": 49, "reference_length": 101}, "bert_score_precision": 0.8575369119644165, "bert_score_recall": 0.8317579030990601, "bert_score_f1": 0.8444507122039795}, "metrics_original": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.21705426356589147, "rouge2": 0.0, "rougeL": 0.15503875968992248, "rougeLsum": 0.20155038759689922}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.3409090909090909, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 0.2737733935931513, "length_ratio": 0.43564356435643564, "translation_length": 44, "reference_length": 101}, "bert_score_precision": 0.82173198461532