{"sample_id": 540, "prompt": "Not sure why, but I don\u2019t like Windows 10. But its hard to explain why", "reference": ", and it might not be even Windows 10\u2019s fault.\nOn-screen keyboard doesn\u2019t pop up automatically for Firefox, but does for Edge (Surface Pro 3 in tablet mode). One assumes because Edge is an Universal App?\nTraditional Chinese keyboard doesn\u2019t display candidate list automatically; you have to press down-arrow every time to see the complete list. That is 1/4 to 1/3 more keystrokes per Chinese character!\nPressing the touchscreen for any action (e.g. close windows, \u2018Ok\u2019 button etc) has a minute but discernible lag, especially if you are used to an iPad. Two finger touchscreen scrolling is great though. Does this lie with Win10 or Surface Pro 3?\nOr maybe I\u2019m just a grumpy old man set in my ways. I will seriously mourn the day Microsoft stops supporting Windows 7.\nIts finally finished. Windows Update has been calculating which updates to apply since 9am. So that\u2019s more than 6 hours to calculate \u2013 now comes the actual update part.\nFair enough, this is a fresh reinstall of Windows 7 on a relic of a CPU: AMD Athlon x2. But its desktop class and not RAM constrained.\nI reckon Windows Update should be the real-world metric to assess how fast a system is. Sure, this way of measuring has a big flaw, since new updates are constantly available so updating at different times will produce different results. Regardless, it\u2019ll still be a good-enough rough measure of how a system would perform for the average person using the PC in real life.", "generated_dual_stream": ", but I don\u2019t like Windows 10. Like windows xp, xp pro, xp and xp pro, xp and xp pro. And also I was using xp and xp pro. And I can\u2019t wait to buy xp and xp pro. And", "generated_original": "in words. I\u2019m sure you will have your own reasons to dislike it. I don\u2019t know what it is, but I don\u2019t like it.\nBut I have no problem with the way it works. It is just different from the previous Windows", "metrics_dual_stream": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.099009900990099, "rouge2": 0.0066445182724252485, "rougeL": 0.052805280528052806, "rougeLsum": 0.07920792079207921}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.3617021276595745, 0.021739130434782608, 0.0, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 0.005805577589194032, "length_ratio": 0.16262975778546712, "translation_length": 47, "reference_length": 289}, "bert_score_precision": 0.834945559501648, "bert_score_recall": 0.7949885129928589, "bert_score_f1": 0.814477264881134}, "metrics_original": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.16286644951140067, "rouge2": 0.006557377049180328, "rougeL": 0.08469055374592832, "rougeLsum": 0.1237785016286645}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.5319148936170213, 0.06521739130434782, 0.0, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 0.005805577589194032, "length_ratio": 0.16262975778546712, "translation_length": 47, "reference_length": 289}, "bert_score_precision": 0.8542702794075012, "bert_score_recall": 0.7979837656021118, "bert_score_f1": 0.825168251991272}, "original_model_loss_on_full_text": 3.2045161724090576}
{"sample_id": 541, "prompt": "How do you find the formula sheet and calculator on the NETA website?\nThe new formula sheet", "reference": " is posted on NETA's website now also(I don't recall it being there before) it's the exact same one I was given. They also have the on screen calculator you use on their website, you can give it a test drive.\nIt's been a while since the exam changed. Have any of the new questions been added to these practice tests?\nWe've been adding new questions in addition to reclassifying others based on what you guys have been posting in the forums. Feel free to send us any questions you would like to see added to help future test takers.\nYou sometimes just need to get lucky. I've heard of guys getting a bunch of relay questions and some getting none. I get why NETA exams are designed the way they are, to force you to know a wide range of things. But the tests should be balanced every time you take it, but it's not.", "generated_dual_stream": "is available on the NETA website, but you can also find the same information in the FAQ section of the NETA website. You can also find the answers to your questions on the NETA website as well as in the FAQ section. The N", "generated_original": "is available on the NETA website under the \u201cMember Resources\u201d tab. In the \u201cMember Benefits\u201d section click on the \u201cFormula Sheet\u201d link. In the \u201cCalculators\u201d section click on the \u201cCalculator\u201d link. In the \u201cCalculator", "metrics_dual_stream": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.25120772946859904, "rouge2": 0.03902439024390243, "rougeL": 0.18357487922705312, "rougeLsum": 0.2222222222222222}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.5957446808510638, 0.13043478260869565, 0.0, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 0.0714828389811092, "length_ratio": 0.27485380116959063, "translation_length": 47, "reference_length": 171}, "bert_score_precision": 0.8686774969100952, "bert_score_recall": 0.8194904923439026, "bert_score_f1": 0.8433673977851868}, "metrics_original": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.16243654822335027, "rouge2": 0.010256410256410256, "rougeL": 0.1218274111675127, "rougeLsum": 0.16243654822335027}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.43243243243243246, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 0.026739280320947717, "length_ratio": 0.21637426900584794, "translation_length": 37, "reference_length": 171}, "bert_score_precision": 0.8193471431732178, "bert_score_recall": 0.8048583269119263, "bert_score_f1": 0.8120381236076355}, "original_model_loss_on_full_text": 2.883345365524292}
{"sample_id": 542, "prompt": "Every contact center and enterprise, whether hosted/ cloud or premise-based, has a unique set of", "reference": " needs. This is why Softdial Contact Center\u2122 (SCC) is designed to be flexible, extensible and scalable, integrating with any legacy equipment, and meeting the most complex of requirements.\nFind the solution for your needs below, or contact us to learn how SCC can meet your requirements.\n(e.g. customer service, technical support, help desk) SCC offers a smooth customer journey through IVR to the right CSR and great service.\n(e.g. telesales, debt collection, market research) Maximise agent talk time and minimise idle time while staying within legal limits for abandoned calls.\nRespond instantly and automatically to service level threats by moving agents freely across campaigns of any media type.\n(e.g. voice, email, chat, social media) Make the most of customer engagement opportunities and maximise agent productivity by using a variety of media.", "generated_dual_stream": "security and will have a independent security solution. This solution is designed to be scalable without sacrificing the appearance of the overall enterprise's workload. Any security problem will have to be solved by contacting center managers, and the owner of the company, as well.", "generated_original": "challenges and opportunities. The industry is experiencing a seismic shift, and companies need to be prepared for this new normal. The future is bright. Contact centers need to be prepared to serve and support their customers in this new environment.\nThis is the future of", "metrics_dual_stream": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.22346368715083798, "rouge2": 0.03389830508474576, "rougeL": 0.1452513966480447, "rougeLsum": 0.20111731843575417}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.007531298175126032, "precisions": [0.46938775510204084, 0.10416666666666667, 0.0425531914893617, 0.021739130434782608], "brevity_penalty": 0.09183561422767024, "length_ratio": 0.29518072289156627, "translation_length": 49, "reference_length": 166}, "bert_score_precision": 0.8528225421905518, "bert_score_recall": 0.8095428347587585, "bert_score_f1": 0.8306192755699158}, "metrics_original": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.21229050279329606, "rouge2": 0.02259887005649717, "rougeL": 0.11173184357541899, "rougeLsum": 0.18994413407821228}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.44, 0.08163265306122448, 0.020833333333333332, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 0.09827358560436154, "length_ratio": 0.30120481927710846, "translation_length": 50, "reference_length": 166}, "bert_score_precision": 0.8546106815338135, "bert_score_recall": 0.8078820705413818, "bert_score_f1": 0.8305896520614624}, "original_model_loss_on_full_text": 2.898946523666382}
{"sample_id": 543, "prompt": "Whether you're a first-time digital video camera user or a budding movie maker, you can count", "reference": " on the Legria range of Canon video cameras to capture special moments and turn them into priceless footage.\nYou'll be able to avoid shaky footage with image stabilisation and automatic ISO will ensure focus is accurately detected and light levels are taken into account. Models in the Canon Legria range enable you to explore your creative side: the Story Creator, Movie Filters and Touch decorations features allow you to add personal touches to captured footage. If you're more experienced and are looking to test your skills or master manual controls, look for the Canon Legria HF G10 or XA10.\nSelect models such as the Canon Legria HF R38, Legria HF R36 and Legria HF M52 also feature Wi-Fi capability. This allows video recordings to be saved wirelessly from your camcorder to a computer in your home network, an FTP server, to YouTube or Facebook, or played back on DLNA-compatible TV sets or media players.", "generated_dual_stream": "on the company to help your brand awareness. We offer a variety of options to suit your business needs.\nWe offer a wide variety of digital marketing services to suit your needs. We offer a wide variety of digital marketing services to suit your needs. We", "generated_original": "on the following tips and tricks to help you get the most from your video camera.\nMake sure your camera is in good condition.\nMake sure you have the latest software for your camera.\nMake sure you have a good internet connection.\nMake sure you have", "metrics_dual_stream": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.1176470588235294, "rouge2": 0.009900990099009901, "rougeL": 0.09803921568627452, "rougeLsum": 0.10784313725490195}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.32, 0.02040816326530612, 0.0, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 0.09632763823049299, "length_ratio": 0.2994011976047904, "translation_length": 50, "reference_length": 167}, "bert_score_precision": 0.8427016735076904, "bert_score_recall": 0.784149706363678, "bert_score_f1": 0.8123720288276672}, "metrics_original": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.18627450980392157, "rouge2": 0.019801980198019802, "rougeL": 0.10784313725490195, "rougeLsum": 0.1568627450980392}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.42, 0.04081632653061224, 0.0, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 0.09632763823049299, "length_ratio": 0.2994011976047904, "translation_length": 50, "reference_length": 167}, "bert_score_precision": 0.8508644104003906, "bert_score_recall": 0.7981339693069458, "bert_score_f1": 0.8236560821533203}, "original_model_loss_on_full_text": 2.8648929595947266}
{"sample_id": 544, "prompt": "San Antonio \u2013 St. Mary\u2019s University baseball players Scott Shimek and Bobby Freeman were named", "reference": " Heartland Conference Pitcher and Hitter of the Week, respectively, it was announced by the league office on Wednesday for their play last weekend against the University of the Incarnate Word.\nShimek (Jr., Shiner) tossed his first shutout of the season, holding the high-powered Incarnate Word offense to just three hits and two walks on Friday. He also struck out four. No Cardinal advanced past second base in the game. The shutout was the first this season against the Cardinals. He improved to 10-0 in 12 starts, with three complete games and one shutout. He has a 3.12 ERA in 80.2 innings of work, with 97 strikeouts against just 31 walks. Opposing batters are hitting just.235 against him.\nFreeman (Sr., Fair Oaks Ranch) hit.538 with three doubles, six RBI and two runs scored against Incarnate Word last weekend. He had hits in three of the four games last week. He also had two hits in two games and three hits in one game. In the first game of the series he went 2-of-4 with a three-run double that helped the Rattlers send the game into extra innings. In the second game of the series he went 2-for-2 with a double, three RBI and two runs scored as the Rattlers cruised to a 9-0 win. He had his second straight perfect game on Saturday, going 3-for-3 with a double. For the season he is batting.327 with seven doubles, two triples, 17 RBI and 23 runs scored. He has 10 games with two or more hits this season.\nThe honors marked the eighth and ninth times this season that a Rattler has been named Heartland Conference Player of the Week. Jonathon Cisneros (So., San Antonio), Jonathon Rosfeld (Fr., San Antonio) and David Vaio (Jr., San Antonio) have been named Heartland Conference Hitter of the Week previously, while Tyler Cales (Jr., San Antonio) and Braxton Watson (Jr., Spring) have been named Heartland Pitcher of the Week this season.\nSt. Mary\u2019s is currently 32-16 overall and 28-12 in Heartland Conference play. The Rattlers will return to action on Friday when they host Lincoln University in the final home series of the season, starting at 2 p.m. at V.J. Keefe Memorial Stadium.", "generated_dual_stream": "Champions League winners for a second time. In 2009 coaches Jason Caswell and Jake Schimeck won the league\u2019s award.\nShimek won 2018-18 after defeating St. Mary\u2019s of Houston 3-2 in a", "generated_original": "to the 2012 Texas Collegiate Baseball All-State team for the 2012 season. The two were joined on the first team by San Antonio\u2019s Christian Castro, a sophomore outfielder for the University of Houston.\nShimek, a", "metrics_dual_stream": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.07600950118764846, "rouge2": 0.01431980906921241, "rougeL": 0.052256532066508314, "rougeLsum": 0.0665083135391924}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.5, 0.13513513513513514, 0.027777777777777776, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 1.7604281454347018e-05, "length_ratio": 0.08370044052863436, "translation_length": 38, "reference_length": 454}, "bert_score_precision": 0.8426896333694458, "bert_score_recall": 0.7655338644981384, "bert_score_f1": 0.8022609949111938}, "metrics_original": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.09929078014184398, "rouge2": 0.028503562945368172, "rougeL": 0.07092198581560284, "rougeLsum": 0.08983451536643028}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.5641025641025641, 0.15789473684210525, 0.05405405405405406, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 2.3914498742222667e-05, "length_ratio": 0.08590308370044053, "translation_length": 39, "reference_length": 454}, "bert_score_precision": 0.8399585485458374, "bert_score_recall": 0.7661230564117432, "bert_score_f1": 0.801343560218811}, "original_model_loss_on_full_text": 1.6354609727859497}
{"sample_id": 545, "prompt": "The DCU Digital Marketing programme was introduced to address the shift in marketing to digital, mobile,", "reference": " and social media, hyper-targeting and feedback of real-time metrics and data leading the way over traditional marketing where interaction information is not as forthcoming.\nThis Digital Marketing programme is designed to help build a management resource pool for the next-generation marketing companies already operating in Ireland (e.g. Facebook, Google, LinkedIn, etc), as well as the evolving requirements of the incumbent marketing industry.\nDesigned in conjunction with both leading industry and academic experts, the programme is designed to meet the requirements of marketing professionals looking to develop their digital marketing skills and knowledge.\nParticipants on the DCU Digital Marketing Programme benefit from a combination of exposure to cutting edge research, academic rigor, industry practice and applied workshop and projects. Lectures are delivered by experienced international and Irish experts from industry and practice.\nOur marketing graduates work in highest echelons of industry worldwide and as alumni of Dublin City University and DCU Business School, students completing the MSc in Digital Marketing become part of this global network and the opportunities for career development and lifelong learning that this represents.", "generated_dual_stream": "and email marketing, and the programme is designed to help both PT and a small businesses to ensure its effectiveness and efficiency. The programme is designed to help you, the business owner to ensure your effectiveness and efficiency. PT and a small businesses can be found", "generated_original": "social media, and the need for students to be digitally literate. The programme offers students an opportunity to develop a wide range of digital skills and knowledge. The programme is also designed to provide students with a solid foundation in digital marketing, which is highly", "metrics_dual_stream": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.22026431718061673, "rouge2": 0.08000000000000002, "rougeL": 0.16740088105726872, "rougeLsum": 0.22026431718061673}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.009782315818556408, "precisions": [0.54, 0.20408163265306123, 0.125, 0.0851063829787234], "brevity_penalty": 0.05286572873835034, "length_ratio": 0.25380710659898476, "translation_length": 50, "reference_length": 197}, "bert_score_precision": 0.8326611518859863, "bert_score_recall": 0.8045928478240967, "bert_score_f1": 0.818386435508728}, "metrics_original": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.247787610619469, "rouge2": 0.08928571428571427, "rougeL": 0.17699115044247787, "rougeLsum": 0.23008849557522124}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.005579046266622264, "precisions": [0.5918367346938775, 0.20833333333333334, 0.06382978723404255, 0.021739130434782608], "brevity_penalty": 0.04878130356189681, "length_ratio": 0.24873096446700507, "translation_length": 49, "reference_length": 197}, "bert_score_precision": 0.8947670459747314, "bert_score_recall": 0.8319284915924072, "bert_score_f1": 0.862204372882843}, "original_model_loss_on_full_text": 2.8330764770507812}
{"sample_id": 546, "prompt": "Rebecca is Co-Founder & CEO at VenueScanner.com.\nVenueScanner has grown rapidly in", "reference": " the past two years recently exceeding 19000 registered venues on the app. This journey hasn\u2019t been easy and Rebecca came on the podcast to discuss bootstrapping this startup. Andy asks why Rebecca wanted to leave the security of a well-paid job to go it alone starting a business and how does she attract the best tech talent to her business.\nVenueScanner.com is the UK\u2019s #1 venue discovery & booking platform, now live in London, Manchester, Edinburgh, Liverpool, Birmingham, Bristol. Their mission is to help you discover venues that you never knew existed \u2013 creative spaces, hidden restaurant, and pub function rooms, iconic school halls, curated public gardens, historical museum spaces and more.\n00.31 A mix between Airbnb and Skyscanner for venues.\n01.58 From investment management to business owner.\n07.52 Why sacrifice a comfortable career to start your own business?\n10.48 Hitting 19000 venues on the VenueScanner app.\n12.22 Dragging independant venues into the 21st century.\n13.40 After hiring 5 people you need to start thinking about culture.\n16.00 How to stand out to candidates in a crowded market.\n18.11 Looking outside of London for talent.\n22.02 The trade-off between time and fundraising.\n24.11 Creating the go-to platform for event planning globally.", "generated_dual_stream": "popularity since its inception in 2007. You can now find it at home or workstations, and is now owned by the University of Wisconsin-Madison. Rebecca has the ability to traverse the country network of offices in the U.S. which", "generated_original": "the past year, and is now one of the largest venues reservation software platforms in the country. Rebecca oversees the company\u2019s technology and creative direction, as well as all business operations.\nRebecca is a graduate of the University of Pennsylvania, and holds a", "metrics_dual_s