{"sample_id": 566, "prompt": "This is much more than the history of skateboard apparel, it is the history of skateboarding including", "reference": " apparel. The authors have taken unbelievable effort to document almost all aspects of the movement, from its roots in the 1950s as an offshoot of surfing culture, through the early 1980s when skateboarding was not connected to surfing anymore and became what it is today. The book features original commentary from designers, company founders, and pro skateboarders who have defined skateboarding\u2019s look for generations. People you meet include Stacy Peralta, Lance Mountain, Tony Alva, Brad Bowman, Steve Olson, Steve Caballero, Steve Van Doren, and many many more.", "generated_dual_stream": "art and architecture. In addition to traditional skateboarding, there is a wide variety of history of skate clothing, including the pop culture, skateboarding. The skateboarding has been the most influential of all, but also a variety of the other skaters", "generated_original": "the history of skateboarding clothes and the history of skateboarding shoes and the history of skateboard trucks and the history of skateboarding equipment and the history of skateboarding and the history of skateboarding in the 80s and the history of skateboarding in", "metrics_dual_stream": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.21875, "rouge2": 0.015873015873015872, "rougeL": 0.109375, "rougeLsum": 0.109375}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.391304347826087, 0.06666666666666667, 0.0, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 0.2960013380148583, "length_ratio": 0.45098039215686275, "translation_length": 46, "reference_length": 102}, "bert_score_precision": 0.8540374040603638, "bert_score_recall": 0.8107465505599976, "bert_score_f1": 0.8318291306495667}, "metrics_original": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.20000000000000004, "rouge2": 0.015625, "rougeL": 0.1846153846153846, "rougeLsum": 0.1846153846153846}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.23809523809523808, 0.024390243902439025, 0.0,