{"sample_id": 809, "prompt": "Anyone who has hosted a party will tell you it\u2019s not as easy as it looks. There", "reference": "\u2019s a lot involved when throwing a party or gathering, and the costs can build up quickly. Getting the best bang for your buck is not only welcomed in the process but strongly desired. Here are a few party rentals that will you keep your costs low and rental value high!\nTransform old items into party decorations with a little elbow grease and creativity. Rent basic tables and tablecloths, and then let your imagination fly! Condiment jars or glasses serve as great makeshift candle holders, and empty wine bottles can always be turned into flower vases. Large tin buckets can be used as ice chests for beverages and old chalkboards can serve as rustic wedding decor. Be creative with unused items around your house and it can help you save money on your special day!\nA prudent way to stick to a food budget is to cook your own and rent chafing dishes to keep your food well-heated throughout your event. Sterno candles can keep your food fresh and warm for up to four hours at a time.\nIf you\u2019re on a tight budget, you may not have the funds to hire servers for your party. An alternative solution is to set up fun concession stands such as a popcorn machine or a chocolate fountain. These concessions are not only a perfect addition to your party, but also a great way to keep your guests entertained without the additional cost of a server.\nStaying within budget can be difficult when planning a party but with some creative thinking and research, you can organize rentals that provide the best bang for your buck. Call A V Party Rentals today to speak with a qualified party expert, who is ready and able to help you create the party you want at a price you can afford.", "generated_dual_stream": "are many different types of parties and a few days before the party, but what to do? The party's starting point is to be able to make sure it\u2019s a success. If you can, the party will stay for a few months, but", "generated_original": "\u2019s a lot to consider and do, and you want to make sure you get everything right. But you can\u2019t do it all on your own. You need a trusted team of experts who can handle every aspect of your event and make it run smoothly", "metrics_dual_stream": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.15954415954415954, "rouge2": 0.045845272206303724, "rougeL": 0.09116809116809117, "rougeLsum": 0.10826210826210826}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.5833333333333334, 0.1702127659574468, 0.021739130434782608, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 0.0030528897843014997, "length_ratio": 0.147239263803681, "translation_length": 48, "reference_length": 326}, "bert_score_precision": 0.8451001644134521, "bert_score_recall": 0.7973427176475525, "bert_score_f1": 0.8205270767211914}, "metrics_original": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.14164305949008496, "rouge2": 0.039886039886039885, "rougeL": 0.0963172804532578, "rougeLsum": 0.11331444759206799}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.5102040816326531, 0.14583333333333334, 0.02127659574468085, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 0.0035067653311051054, "length_ratio": 0.15030674846625766, "translation_length": 49, "reference_length": 326}, "bert_score_precision": 0.8688062429428101, "bert_score_recall": 0.8044952154159546, "bert_score_f1": 0.8354148864746094}, "original_model_loss_on_full_text": 2.4809072017669678}
{"sample_id": 810, "prompt": "Enter Edem turned the Abbey Park ruins and historic gardens into a Medieval and Victorian Extravagan", "reference": "za to tell the the story of Abbey Park. Families of all cultures and ages benefited from the free zany activities, learning whilst having fun! Henry the Eighth will ask the question \u2018Who killed Cardinal Wosley?\u2019 on a Monk murder mystery tour alongside live jousting and life size Alice in Wonderland chess games \u2026 and more! Dog friendly. Suitable for all cultures and ages. Welcoming the whole community.\nPhoto\u2019s by the very talented Jonathan Macauley of Abbey Park Extravaganza 2017!", "generated_dual_stream": "za! Open to the public, the events are open to all ages. The Abbey Park has a great old-fashioned charm and the events that took place there are from medieval times to Victorian street lights in the 1860\u2019s. In addition to various", "generated_original": "za with a great line-up of musicians, dancers, actors, costumed characters and food trucks.\nThe day included a parade of Medieval costumed characters, a Medieval Jousting competition, medieval games, a medieval market, and a great Medieval and", "metrics_dual_stream": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.25806451612903225, "rouge2": 0.01639344262295082, "rougeL": 0.19354838709677416, "rougeLsum": 0.22580645161290322}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.391304347826087, 0.044444444444444446, 0.0, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 0.3842270061816404, "length_ratio": 0.5111111111111111, "translation_length": 46, "reference_length": 90}, "bert_score_precision": 0.8553587794303894, "bert_score_recall": 0.8309105634689331, "bert_score_f1": 0.8429574370384216}, "metrics_original": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.1694915254237288, "rouge2": 0.0, "rougeL": 0.15254237288135591, "rougeLsum": 0.1694915254237288}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.2222222222222222, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 0.36787944117144233, "length_ratio": 0.5, "translation_length": 45, "reference_