{"sample_id": 859, "prompt": "Science Communication\u2026 I think that is something we all hope we are doing, communicating the science with", "reference": " our clientele. Today I came across this article that has paired the temperature effects of global warming to music. While I do not have a musical ear at all, I do think it is interesting that the article/video talks about communicating science, and that through using music people may understand the science better \u2013 just by changing the way the message is delivered. Wow! So as food for thought, have you thought about how you can/are changing the way your messages are delivered to your clientele so they can understand the science?\nLink | This entry was posted in Delivery Strategies, Teaching and tagged Communication, music, science. Bookmark the permalink.\nI really will need to\u2026HaHa). You certainly put a brand new spin on a topic that\u2019s been discussed for ages. Excellent stuff, just excellent!", "generated_dual_stream": "respect to issues such as these.\nI believe this is something that I hope we all wish to do.\nCommunication of course through the internet. I hope you enjoyed this site and found it to be informative at least. I hope that you enjoyed communicating the", "generated_original": "the public. It\u2019s a job that is very rewarding and I would love to do it. I would like to give back to the community and help people understand science. I think the best way to do that is to give back to the community and", "metrics_dual_stream": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.2857142857142857, "rouge2": 0.0, "rougeL": 0.14285714285714285, "rougeLsum": 0.2087912087912088}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.56, 0.02040816326530612, 0.0, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 0.12003162851145678, "length_ratio": 0.32051282051282054, "translation_length": 50, "reference_length": 156}, "bert_score_precision": 0.8413087129592896, "bert_score_recall": 0.7926366925239563, "bert_score_f1": 0.8162477612495422}, "metrics_original"