{"sample_id": 860, "prompt": "At Forest Hills Wesleyan Church, we count it a blessing to have you worship with us.", "reference": " We are located on the corner of Barker Avenue and Claremont Avenue in Evansville, IN. We are a family friendly church and endeavor to assure all of our guest feel welcome and connected when they visit with us.\nFeel free to join us in worship on Sunday morning. Sunday School begins at 9:30am and worship services begin at 10:30am. Nursery is available for children through two years old. Children's classes are also available. Greeters will be happy to help you find a seat and direct you to class locations.\n\u200bClick HERE for directions and a map.\nClick HERE for more information about service times.\nClick HERE for more information about our Life Groups and how you can get connected with e group of people seeking God.\nWe hope you will join us soon. Feel free to contact our Church office.", "generated_dual_stream": "Our worship ends when the Bible says we should do so. We believe worship is expected to be a blessing. It is a blessing to us and to others. We believe worship is expected to be our \u2018best\u2019 way of service to God. There", "generated_original": "You are welcome to join us any Sunday morning or Wednesday evening. We believe that we are all created by God, and that we are all created to have a relationship with Him. We are here to worship God and to glorify Him in everything we", "metrics_dual_stream": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.2459893048128342, "rouge2": 0.0, "rougeL": 0.12834224598930483, "rougeLsum": 0.19251336898395724}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.5208333333333334, 0.06382978723404255, 0.0, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 0.1032261224620199, "length_ratio": 0.3057324840764331, "translation_length": 48, "reference_length": 157}, "bert_score_precision": 0.8443571329116821, "bert_score_recall": 0.7995650172233582, "bert_score_f1": 0.8213509321212769}, "metrics_original": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.26455026455026454, "rouge2": 0.053475935828877004, "rougeL": 0.14814814814814817, "rougeLsum": 0.21164021164021166}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.5102040816326531, 0.125, 0.0425531914893617, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 0.11035182229371183, "length_ratio": 0.31210191082802546, "translation_length": 49, "reference_length": 157}, "bert_score_precision": 0.8711485862731934, "bert_score_recall": 0.8259353637695312, "bert_score_f1": 0.847939670085907}, "original_model_loss_on_full_text": 2.1177263259887695}
{"sample_id": 861, "prompt": "This is the third in a series of six-week-long research workshops on Machine Learning for Speech Language", "reference": " and Computer Vision Technology. These workshops bring together diverse \u201cdream teams\u201d of leading professionals, graduate students, and undergraduates, in a truly cooperative, intensive, and substantive effort to advance the state of the science.\nThese workshops constitute a continuation of the well known Johns Hopkins University summer workshops, and encompasses all areas of human language technology including automatic speech recognition, natural language processing, machine translation, topic detection and tracking, information retrieval and extraction, summarization and question answering, and certain related areas of computer vision, including image understanding and visual scene analysis. These fields share many important algorithmic and statistical approaches, allowing cross-fertilization. Machine learning challenges that arise from these areas are of fundamental scientific interest, and are shared with many other fields of science and engineering, such as medical-/bio-informatics and social network analysis.\nThe Center for Language and Speech Processing at Johns Hopkins University (JHU) has 20 years of experience with organizing workshops of this kind. JHU will therefore act as an anchor for these workshops, but the actual host institution will rotate from year to year in order to ensure wider community ownership and engagement, and to distribute the organizational burden more widely. The 2014 workshop was hosted at Charles University in Prague, the 2015 workshop was hosted at the University of Washington in Seattle, WA, and Johns Hopkins University in Baltimore, MD, will be the site of the 2016 workshop.", "generated_dual_stream": "Pathology which are lecture and practice oriented. These workshops are meant for graduate students who are working on placing in the field of Speech Language Pathology. The workshops will be held in a short two-week period, with two lectures, and two practice sessions", "generated_original": "Processing (ML-SSLP). This workshop will cover the topics of Deep Learning, Convolutional Neural Networks, and Autoencoders. The first two weeks of this workshop will be devoted to theoretical and practical aspects of these topics.\nThe third week", "metrics_dual_stream": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.15107913669064746, "rouge2": 0.028985507246376812, "rougeL": 0.10791366906474818, "rougeLsum": 0.11510791366906477}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.5319148936170213, 0.15217391304347827, 0.022222222222222223, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 0.009470491540786222, "length_ratio": 0.17669172932330826, "translation_length": 47, "reference_length": 266}, "bert_score_precision": 0.8464565277099609, "bert_score_recall": 0.8027395009994507, "bert_score_f1": 0.8240185379981995}, "metrics_original": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.1323529411764706, "rouge2": 0.014814814814814814, "rougeL": 0.08823529411764706, "rougeLsum": 0.11029411764705882}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.5454545454545454, 0.11627906976744186, 0.0, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 0.0064385330926608805, "length_ratio": 0.16541353383458646, "translation_length": 44, "reference_length": 266}, "bert_score_precision": 0.8545117378234863, "bert_score_recall": 0.8085075616836548, "bert_score_f1": 0.8308733701705933}, "original_model_loss_on_full_text": 2.418654441833496}
