{"sample_id": 936, "prompt": "UCLA quarterback Josh Rosen's hot streak continued on Saturday, as he threw for 329 yards", "reference": " and five touchdowns in a 56-23 win over Hawaii at the Rose Bowl in Pasadena, California.\nSince trailing 38-10 at halftime against Texas A&M in the season opener on Sept. 3, Rosen has looked like one of the nation's best quarterbacks.\nOver his past six quarters, Rosen has thrown for 710 yards and all nine of his touchdowns. The junior has yet to throw an interception in 84 pass attempts.\nPer ESPN Stats & Info, Rosen became the first Pac-12 quarterback to have a game with at least 300 passing yards, five touchdowns and a completion percentage of at least 85 percent in 20 years.\nIt's felt like just a matter of time before Rosen has his breakout season for the Bruins. He came to UCLA with otherworldly hype as a 5-star recruit and top-ranked pro-style quarterback in the 2015 recruiting class, per Scout.com.\nA shoulder injury limited Rosen to just six games in 2016, but he's shown no lingering effects through two starts this season.", "generated_dual_stream": "and three touchdowns. Rosenthal trailed 24 points in the dot-throwing game, 2010.6 points in the third quarter.\nThis entry was posted on March 23rd and tagged UCLA, UCLA on March 23. Bookmark the", "generated_original": "and four touchdowns in the Bruins' 52-7 rout of Idaho. Rosen had a perfect passer rating of 158.3 in the victory, and finished with a 75.4 completion percentage. He also had 42 rushes for 142", "metrics_dual_stream": {"rouge": {"rouge1": 0.12322274881516589, "rouge2": 0.019138755980861247, "rougeL": 0.0947867298578199, "rougeLsum": 0.12322274881516589}, "bleu": {"bleu": 0.0, "precisions": [0.4473684210526316, 0.08108108108108109, 0.0, 0.0], "brevity_penalty": 0.017376586559077603, "length_ratio": 0.19791666666666666, "translation_length": 38, "reference_length": 192}, "bert_score_precision": 0.79618239402771, "bert_score_recall": 0.7875330448150635, "bert_sco